Closes: 1131896
Changes:
 python3.11 (3.11.2-6+deb12u9) bookworm-security; urgency=medium
 .
   * Non-maintainer upload by the LTS Team.
   * Apply upstream patches for the following CVEs:
     - CVE-2025-69534: Treat invalid markup declarations in
       html.parser.HTMLParser as bogus comments instead of raising
       AssertionError (Closes: #1131896)
     - CVE-2026-1502: Reject CR/LF in HTTP tunnel request headers
     - CVE-2026-3276: Fix O(n^2) canonical ordering in unicodedata.normalize()
     - CVE-2026-6019: Percent-encode the cookie embedded in JavaScript by
       http.cookies.Morsel.js_output() and decode it with decodeURIComponent()
     - CVE-2026-8328: Apply CVE-2021-4189 PASV fix to ftplib.ftpcp()
     - CVE-2026-9669: Prevent bz2 decompressor reuse after errors
     - CVE-2026-15308: Accumulate data passed to html.parser.HTMLParser.feed()
       and only parse again once the unparsed buffer has doubled
     - CVE-2026-15310: Bound zipfile decompression for bzip2/LZMA/Zstandard
     - CVE-2026-15806: Scope HTTPPasswordMgr credentials by URL scheme
     - CVE-2026-17084: Don't consider Unicode codepoint attributes outside
       RFC 3454
     - CVE-2026-18503: Match quoted fields in csv.Sniffer.sniff() without
       backtracking (fixes quadratic time)
     - CVE-2026-19445: Do not call the servername callback through a released
       SSLContext (fixes use-after-free)
     - CVE-2026-19553: Validate SSLContext.wrap_bio() parameters like
       wrap_socket(). Raise a DeprecationWarning instead of ValueError.
   * Apply further upstream patches the ones above depend on:
     - gh-100061, gh-106052: Fix bug in the matching of possessive
       quantifiers: restore the global Input Stream pointer after trying to
       match a sub-pattern
     - gh-135661: Fix parsing start and end tags in HTMLParser according to
       the HTML5 standard. Includes test.support.subTests() used by the test
       for CVE-2026-17084.
   * Match whole fields when detecting doubled quotes in csv.Sniffer.sniff()
     preventing exponential backtracking (gh-109638).
